# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Since 2026-11-08 these files live OUTSIDE the repo, in $XDG_STATE_HOME/quicktest/secrets/
# (scripts/qspaths.py moves an old copy there on first use). The lines below stay so a
# copy left behind by an older version, or restored by hand, still can't be committed.
#
# discord-rpc.json carries the OAuth `clientSecret` (32 chars, currently set) and is
# written 0600 by scripts/discord-credentials.py — which exists precisely so the secret
# never passes through argv or QML. Committing it would undo all of that, and this repo
# is PUBLISHED, so a single push would put it in the clone history of everyone who has
# ever pulled it.
#
# Anyone setting this config up creates their own via the Discord page in settings.
discord-rpc.json

# ai-keys.json holds the launcher's AI provider API keys, written 0600 by
# scripts/ai-credentials.py for exactly the same reasons. It lands in this directory
# because $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/quicktest IS this repo — so without this line a key would
# sit untracked-but-visible in `git status`, one `git add -A` from being published.
ai-keys.json

# cs2-gsi.json is scripts/install-cs2-gsi.sh's record of the port and auth token it
# wrote into CS2's Game State Integration .cfg, written 0600. The token is only a
# loopback shared secret and regenerated on every install, so it's far less sensitive
# than the two above — but it's still a generated per-machine value that belongs in
# nobody else's clone, and $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/quicktest IS this repo.
cs2-gsi.json

# lyrics-translate-keys.json holds the DeepL API key used by the lyrics-translation
# fallback, written 0600 by scripts/lyrics-translate-credentials.py for exactly the
# same reasons ai-keys.json is gitignored above — a personal API key must never
# round-trip through a config someone else forks.
lyrics-translate-keys.json

# games.json is the Games module's per-user record: your custom entries, per-profile
# settings and PLAY-TIME stats. Personal, rewritten as you play, and not something a
# clone should inherit.
games.json

# ── Machine-local agent/editor settings ───────────────────────────────────────
# settings.local.json holds absolute /home paths. .claude/settings.json (shared) and
# .claude/skills/ are intentionally NOT ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Python bytecode ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ── Editor and OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.swp
*~
*.bak
.DS_Store

# ── The blobs plugin's build tree ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/build-blobs-plugin.sh compiles here; the INSTALLED module goes to the
# system Qt QML dir (see the script), so nothing under plugin/build is ever what
# ships — it's exactly the kind of machine-specific binary output the rest of
# this file's rules exist to keep out. A CMakeCache.txt that rides along in a
# clone has another machine's paths baked in and breaks the next build; the
# script rm -rf's this dir before configuring for that reason.
plugin/build/

# ── Deliberately NOT ignored, so the reasoning is on the record ───────────────
#   presets/bar.json      meant to be read, hand-edited, shared and backed up
#   presets/cursor.json   the same, for the cursor's saved looks (created on first Save)
#   shaders/*.qsb         compiled at build time, but nothing here rebuilds it —
#                         drop it and the liquid-glass effect silently stops working
#   colorschemes/         the user's saved schemes; small, and the point of saving them
#
# The live preferences document is NOT here at all: it lives in XDG_STATE_HOME
# (Quickshell.statePath("config.json")), deliberately outside the shell directory,
# because it is rewritten on every slider drag and watchFiles would reload on each one.
